Z||000000||87fiero_gt||07-07-99||10:33 PM||||I have two marks on my balancer. A wide one about 1/4 inch wide and a thin one. Does anybody else have these? What is the scope tube for on the timing pointer?
Z||000001||FieroMike||07-08-99||06:55 AM||||My balancer had one wide one and two thin ones, the wide one is the timing mark.  Scope Tube?
Z||000002||87fiero_gt||07-08-99||08:02 AM||||There is like a sight tube on the right side of the timing pointer. It looks to me that it is just right of zero. Maybe its on zero?<br>I really have a hard time seeing the numbers on the pointer.
Z||000003||87fiero_gt||07-08-99||09:06 AM||||I received some info on a way us Fiero owners could get some $$ help. Maybe help us afford repairs while we are on the web. At no cost. If anybody is interested email me.
Z||000004||theogre||07-08-99||10:16 AM||||That tube appears on allot of cars, from allot of makers. It holds a sensor that is used to test the engine at the factory from what I can find out.
Z||000005||87fiero_gt||07-08-99||11:04 AM||||Thanks for the info. I was hoping it didn't have to do with how I set the timing.
Z||000006||PaUL||07-08-99||02:19 PM||||I always wondered what that tube was for.
Z||000007||GREENDANO||07-08-99||06:16 PM||||That tube on the timing cover is far a magnetic pick-up to measure engine timing.  If you've ever had your car put on a diagnostic scope and had the full gammit of tests done that's where the analyzer got the timing input.<br>  Dan-O
